  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The acceleration vector shall change the component of velocity u<sub>II</sub> along the acceleration vector.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>a</mi><mtext>n</mtext></msub></mfrac></math><br /><br />The radius of curvature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub></math>means v is minimum and a<sub>n</sub> is maximum. This is at the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> when the component of velocity parallel to the acceleration vector becomes zero, that is u<sub>II</sub> = 0.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0021277_AnsExp_1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 313px; height: 203px;\" /><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;&#160;&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mo>&#8869;</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mtext>&#160;m</mtext></math>",
